  "text": " as it appeared on June 9th, 2020, old ID version 963474218, read by myself, user Arlo Barnes, on June 21st, 2020. Chiptune, from Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia, for the altering of car electronics, see Chiptuning. Chiptune, also known as chip music, is a style of synthesized electronic music made using the programmable sound generator, PSG sound chips or synthesizers, in vintage arcade machines, computers, and video game consoles. The term is commonly used to refer to tracker format music, which intentionally sounds similar to older PSG-created music.",
